---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="Two uses of randomness with a seeded generator, so every run repeats. Top: quicksort counted in comparisons. Bottom: keep a few items from a stream, counted over many runs. Nothing is timed.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Start with <b>Input order</b> "Sorted", <b>Number of items</b> <b>1,000</b>, <b>Pivot rule</b> "First element" and <b>Seed</b> <b>1</b>: the worst case, <b>499,500</b> comparisons. Set <b>Pivot rule</b> to "Random pivot": <b>10,187</b> comparisons, and over seeds 1 to 20 the count ranges from <b>10,113</b> to <b>11,960</b>, mean <b>10,865</b>.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Number of items</b> to <b>10,000</b>: random pivot costs <b>154,586</b> comparisons. Set <b>Pivot rule</b> to "First element": <b>49,995,000</b>. Then set <b>Input order</b> to "Shuffled": <b>146,101</b>. Set <b>Pivot rule</b> back to "Random pivot": <b>160,879</b>. Randomness costs a little on easy input and buys a guarantee on hard input.</li>
    <li>In the sampling box, with <b>Sampling rule</b> "Reservoir", <b>Stream length</b> <b>10</b> and <b>Sample size</b> <b>3</b>, over <b>10,000</b> runs every item is kept between <b>2,915</b> and <b>3,071</b> times, close to the fair <b>3,000</b>.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Sampling rule</b> to "Naive: replace a random cell half the time": the counts spread from <b>1,679</b> to <b>4,928</b>, and later items are favoured. Set it to "First k only": the first 3 items are always kept (<b>10,000</b> times) and the rest never.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg rs" data-rs>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Input order <select class="pg-in" data-order><option value="sorted" selected>Sorted</option><option value="shuffled">Shuffled</option></select></label>
      <label>Number of items <select class="pg-in" data-n><option value="100">100</option><option value="1000" selected>1,000</option><option value="10000">10,000</option></select></label>
      <label>Pivot rule <select class="pg-in" data-rule><option value="first" selected>First element</option><option value="random">Random pivot</option></select></label>
      <label>Seed <input class="pg-in" type="number" data-seed value="1" min="1" max="1000" step="1" style="width: 6em" /></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-c1><h3>Comparisons</h3><span class="pg-mono rs-big" data-comp></span><span class="pg-note" data-compn></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Worst case, n(n-1)/2</h3><span class="pg-mono rs-big" data-worst></span><span class="pg-note" data-worstn></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Seeds 1 to 20: lowest</h3><span class="pg-mono rs-big" data-low></span><span class="pg-note">only the random pivot depends on the seed</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Seeds 1 to 20: highest</h3><span class="pg-mono rs-big" data-high></span><span class="pg-note" data-mean></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-qverdict role="status"></p>
    <h3>Sampling from a stream</h3>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Sampling rule <select class="pg-in" data-srule><option value="reservoir" selected>Reservoir (Algorithm R)</option><option value="naive">Naive: replace a random cell half the time</option><option value="first">First k only</option></select></label>
      <label>Stream length <select class="pg-in" data-slen><option value="10" selected>10</option><option value="20">20</option></select></label>
      <label>Sample size <select class="pg-in" data-k><option value="2">2</option><option value="3" selected>3</option><option value="5">5</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>Times each item was kept, over 10,000 runs</h3>
      <div class="rs-cols" data-cols></div>
      <span class="pg-note" data-axis></span>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Fair share</h3><span class="pg-mono rs-big" data-fair></span><span class="pg-note">runs x sample size / stream length</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-s2><h3>Lowest count</h3><span class="pg-mono rs-big" data-slow></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-s3><h3>Highest count</h3><span class="pg-mono rs-big" data-shigh></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-sverdict role="status"></p>
    <p class="pg-note" data-one></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Assumptions: the generator is x = x * 16807 mod 2,147,483,647 (the Park-Miller minimal standard), chosen so the arithmetic stays exact in any language; the tiny modulo bias is ignored. Keys are distinct. A comparison is one element tested against the pivot. Sampling runs share one generator seeded with 7.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, formatThousands } from '../playground';
  const MOD = 2147483647;
  // The same model as the code samples, ported to TypeScript.
  function makeRng(seed: number) {
    let x = seed;
    return (m: number) => { x = (x * 16807) % MOD; return x % m; };
  }
  function shuffled(n: number, seed: number): number[] {
    const a = Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => i + 1);
    const rand = makeRng(seed);
    for (let i = n - 1; i > 0; i--) { const j = rand(i + 1); const t = a[i]; a[i] = a[j]; a[j] = t; }
    return a;
  }
  function quicksort(input: number[], rule: string, seed: number): number {
    const a = input.slice();
    const rand = makeRng(seed);
    let comparisons = 0;
    const stack: [number, number][] = [[0, a.length - 1]];
    while (stack.length) {
      const [lo, hi] = stack.pop()!;
      if (lo >= hi) continue;
      if (rule === 'random') { const p = lo + rand(hi - lo + 1); const t = a[lo]; a[lo] = a[p]; a[p] = t; }
      const pivot = a[lo];
      let i = lo;
      for (let j = lo + 1; j <= hi; j++) {
        comparisons++;
        if (a[j] < pivot) { i++; const t = a[i]; a[i] = a[j]; a[j] = t; }
      }
      const t = a[lo]; a[lo] = a[i]; a[i] = t;
      stack.push([lo, i - 1], [i + 1, hi]);
    }
    return comparisons;
  }
  function sample(n: number, k: number, rule: string, rand: (m: number) => number) {
    const cells: number[] = [];
    let writes = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      const item = i + 1;
      if (i < k) { cells.push(item); writes++; continue; }
      if (rule === 'reservoir') { const j = rand(i + 1); if (j < k) { cells[j] = item; writes++; } }
      else if (rule === 'naive') { if (rand(2) === 0) { cells[rand(k)] = item; writes++; } }
    }
    return { cells, writes };
  }
  const TRIALS = 10000;

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-rs]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const val = (s: string) => q<HTMLInputElement | HTMLSelectElement>(s).value;
    const colour = (s: string, c: string) => q<HTMLElement>(s).style.setProperty('--c', c);

    function drawSort() {
      const order = val('[data-order]'), n = Number(val('[data-n]')), rule = val('[data-rule]');
      const seed = Math.min(1000, Math.max(1, Math.floor(Number(val('[data-seed]'))) || 1));
      const input = order === 'sorted' ? Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => i + 1) : shuffled(n, 99);
      const comp = quicksort(input, rule, seed);
      const worst = (n * (n - 1)) / 2;
      q('[data-comp]').textContent = formatThousands(comp);
      q('[data-compn]').textContent = rule === 'first' ? 'first element as pivot: no randomness' : `random pivot, seed ${seed}`;
      colour('[data-c1]', comp >= worst * 0.9 ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      q('[data-worst]').textContent = formatThousands(worst);
      q('[data-worstn]').textContent = `${Math.round((comp * 100) / worst)}% of it in this run`;
      let low = Infinity, high = 0, total = 0;
      for (let s = 1; s <= 20; s++) { const c = quicksort(input, 'random', s); low = Math.min(low, c); high = Math.max(high, c); total += c; }
      q('[data-low]').textContent = formatThousands(low);
      q('[data-high]').textContent = formatThousands(high);
      q('[data-mean]').textContent = `mean ${formatThousands(Math.floor(total / 20))} over 20 seeds of the random pivot`;
      q('[data-qverdict]').textContent = comp >= worst * 0.9
        ? `The first element is a bad pivot on sorted input: every partition peels off one item, so the work is about n squared / 2. Anyone who can control the input order controls the cost.`
        : rule === 'random'
          ? `A random pivot has no bad input, only bad luck: 20 seeds on this very input stay between ${formatThousands(low)} and ${formatThousands(high)}. The expected cost is about n log n, and the worst case is still possible but astronomically unlikely.`
          : `On shuffled input the first element happens to be fine: the shape of the input is doing the work that the random pivot would otherwise do.`;
    }

    function drawSample() {
      const rule = val('[data-srule]'), n = Number(val('[data-slen]')), k = Number(val('[data-k]'));
      const rand = makeRng(7);
      const counts = new Array<number>(n).fill(0);
      for (let t = 0; t < TRIALS; t++) for (const item of sample(n, k, rule, rand).cells) counts[item - 1]++;
      const fair = (TRIALS * k) / n;
      const lo = Math.min(...counts), hi = Math.max(...counts);
      const cols = q('[data-cols]');
      cols.textContent = '';
      const top = Math.max(1, hi, fair);
      counts.forEach((c, i) => {
        const col = document.createElement('div'); col.className = 'rs-col';
        const bar = document.createElement('span'); bar.className = 'rs-bar'; bar.style.height = `${Math.max(1, (c / top) * 100)}%`;
        bar.style.background = Math.abs(c - fair) <= fair * 0.1 ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)';
        bar.title = `item ${i + 1}: ${formatThousands(c)}`;
        const lab = document.createElement('span'); lab.className = 'rs-lab'; lab.textContent = String(i + 1);
        col.append(bar, lab); cols.appendChild(col);
      });
      q('[data-axis]').textContent = `Items 1 to ${n}, left to right. Green: within 10% of the fair share of ${formatThousands(fair)}.`;
      q('[data-fair]').textContent = formatThousands(fair);
      q('[data-slow]').textContent = formatThousands(lo);
      q('[data-shigh]').textContent = formatThousands(hi);
      const fairRun = hi - lo <= fair * 0.2;
      colour('[data-s2]', fairRun ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      colour('[data-s3]', fairRun ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q('[data-sverdict]').textContent = rule === 'reservoir'
        ? `Fair: item i (after the first ${k}) is kept with chance ${k}/i at the moment it arrives, and each later item then evicts it with exactly the chance that keeps every item at ${k}/${n}. The spread you see is ordinary sampling noise.`
        : rule === 'naive'
          ? `Biased: a later item only has to win one coin flip, an early one has to survive them all, so recent items are kept far more often. It looks random and is not uniform.`
          : `Not a sample at all: the first ${k} items are always kept and the others never. Cheap, deterministic and badly biased if the stream has any order.`;
      const one = sample(1000000, 5, 'reservoir', makeRng(2024));
      q('[data-one]').textContent = `Memory: a reservoir keeps ${k} cells whatever the stream length. One pass over 1,000,000 items with a sample of 5 (seed 2024) keeps [${one.cells.map(formatThousands).join(', ')}] after only ${one.writes} writes; loading all items to shuffle them would need 1,000,000 cells.`;
    }

    root.addEventListener('change', () => { drawSort(); drawSample(); });
    root.addEventListener('input', (e) => { if ((e.target as HTMLElement).matches('[data-seed]')) drawSort(); });
    drawSort(); drawSample();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .rs .pg-note, .playground .rs .pg-out, .playground .how li { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .playground .rs-big { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .playground .rs-cols { overflow: hidden; display: flex; gap: 4px; align-items: flex-end; height: 120px; }
  .playground .rs-col { flex: 1; min-width: 0; height: 100%; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: flex-end; align-items: center; gap: 2px; }
  .playground .rs-bar { display: block; width: 100%; border-radius: 3px 3px 0 0; }
  .playground .rs-lab { overflow: hidden; max-width: 100%; font-size: 0.7rem; color: var(--muted); height: 1em; }
</style>
